<h2>Planning around India's own supply position</h2>
<p>Because India's own lentil production doesn't always cover domestic demand, masoor availability for export can tighten in years when Indian domestic prices rise and government policy responds by prioritising domestic supply. This isn't a constant risk, but it's a genuine one worth building into any long-term Bangladesh masoor programme — diversifying your supplier relationships and maintaining some flexibility in order timing gives you more room to manage a tighter-supply year without disruption to your own downstream business.</p>
